# Draft-commit style.md (persistent)

This file was written by `/draft-commit-message` when you chose **style.md, this commit and onward**.

When drafting or creating commits in this repo:

- Follow `.cursor/skills/draft-commit-message/references/style.md`.
- Do not use Conventional Commits prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- Do not ask whether to use that style. It stays on until this rule is removed.

**To stop and get the once/onward prompt again:** delete this file (`.cursor/rules/draft-commit-style.mdc`). Nothing else to undo.

Only one draft-commit persist rule should exist. If `.cursor/rules/draft-commit-gitlog.mdc` (or a legacy `gitkraken-commit-*.mdc`) is also present, delete one of them.
